# Shaz Agency Web Design Engine — Agent Directives

Strictly adhere to the 18 Universal Design Laws for all frontend engineering:
- Law 1: Zero Fluff Text
- Law 2: Zero Badges, Pills & Eyebrows
- Law 3: Category-Driven Color Freedom (Strict Neon Prohibition)
- Law 4: Zero Generic Templates, AI Clichés, or Dry Wireframes
- Law 5: Zero Third-Party Branding
- Law 6: Zero Emojis & Mandatory Monochrome Vector Icons
- Law 7: Zero Comment Leaks & Clean Background Media
- Law 8: Selective Surface Hierarchy (Never Force Universal Double-Bezel)
- Law 9: Zero Post-Hero Telemetry Ticker Strips
- Law 10: Seamless Atmospheric Section Transitions
- Law 11: Hero Elements Purity (Strictly Backgroundless & Calm)
- Law 12: Bespoke Non-Classic Footers
- Law 13: Absolute Prohibition of Eyebrows & Overlines
- Law 14: Isolated Transparent Imagery (Zero Boxed Photo Frames)
- Law 15: Page Architecture Modality (One-Page vs Multi-Page Routing)
- Law 16: Scroll-Morphing Collapsible Dock Navigation (Deterministic CSS Scoping)
- Law 17: Ecosystem & Technology Integration Infinite Marquee
- Law 18: Bespoke Vector Favicon Architecture

Available Slash Commands:
- /shaz [brief]: Master autonomous design engine
- /shaz-audit: 16-point quality gate audit runner
- /shaz-hero: Backgroundless, high-cinematic hero generator
- /shaz-3d: 141 WebGL and Three.js shader stage generator
- /shaz-style: 40 Authentic web style synthesizers
- /shaz-dock: Kinetic scroll-morphing collapsible dock navigation
- /shaz-component: 114 NameThatUI dictionary components

When executing any command, provide structured architectural explanations before presenting complete, unabridged, production-grade code.
